<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Auto Backup rules for Android 11 and below (this file is ignored on Android 12+, which uses
    data_extraction_rules.xml - keep the two include lists identical).

    POLICY (Phase 8, Step 22): an explicit ALLOWLIST. When <include> is present, Android backs up ONLY the
    included files and nothing else, so everything not listed (voucher attachments, generated PDFs, secure
    prefs, Crashlytics/Firebase state, cache) is excluded by omission. Android lint rejects an <exclude> that is
    not inside an included path, so only the database side-files (inside the included db path) are excluded
    explicitly; BackupPolicyTest asserts that every other sensitive path is NOT covered by any include.

    - The MAIN database file only. The -wal/-shm files are never backed up: copied as separate files they
      could be out of step with the main file and restore as a corrupt database; the main file alone is a
      consistent (possibly slightly older) state because every accounting write is one transaction.
    - The Keystore-backed secure prefs and their Tink keyset are never backed up: the Android Keystore key is
      not restored, so a restored copy would be unreadable (and SecureStorage would silently fall back to a
      plaintext file). A restored app simply starts with fresh secure prefs.
    - Voucher attachments and generated documents (receipts, PAN/Aadhaar/GST scans a user attached) are not
      backed up.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <include domain="database" path="ledgerprime_accounting.db" />
    <include domain="sharedpref" path="ledgerprime_automation_cycle_prefs.xml" />

    <exclude domain="database" path="ledgerprime_accounting.db-wal" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="ledgerprime_accounting.db-shm" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="ledgerprime_accounting.db-journal" />
</full-backup-content>